WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:05.200
So what can a few minutes of unplanned downtime&nbsp;
cost a business? Six or seven figures in lost&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:13.120
revenue? A damaged brand? Regulatory action? Hi,&nbsp;
my name is Albert Traylor and I'm with IBM&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.120 --> 00:00:21.760
Cloud, and today I'm here to talk about artificial&nbsp;
intelligence for operations, also known as AIOps.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.280 --> 00:00:26.960
So before we go into the definition of&nbsp;
AIOps, let's think about a scenario.

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:31.440
Imagine that you are an it operations professional&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.440 --> 00:00:36.400
at a successful real estate company.&nbsp;
Let's call that company "Housing For All."&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.320 --> 00:00:45.840
At h4a you support a portfolio of applications&nbsp;
one of which is an invoicing application used by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.840 --> 00:00:53.040
tens of thousands of partners every day. For this&nbsp;
specific application your focus is to make sure&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:58.800
it's up and that partners can deliver&nbsp;
invoices consistently on it on a regular basis.

00:00:59.760 --> 00:01:04.160
One day you settle into your desk you get&nbsp;
a cup of coffee and you get a phone call,&nbsp;

00:01:04.160 --> 00:01:09.920
just like that. Out of nowhere a sales rep is&nbsp;
calling to complain that a partner is trying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.920 --> 00:01:14.400
to upload an invoice and has been unable to&nbsp;
all morning because the application is down.

00:01:15.120 --> 00:01:18.960
What do you do in that scenario to get&nbsp;
this application back up and running?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.920 --> 00:01:26.560
So before we continue down that scenario let's&nbsp;
talk about AIOps and the textbook definition.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:32.720
Artificial intelligence for operations is about&nbsp;
the application of artificial intelligence&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.720 --> 00:01:39.280
machine learning models and advanced&nbsp;
analytics to IT operational data. The objective&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.280 --> 00:01:45.440
is to empower it professionals and operations&nbsp;
professionals with the data they need to make&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.440 --> 00:01:50.160
decisions and ultimately resolve and&nbsp;
restore service to an application&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.160 --> 00:01:58.160
faster. So with that definition in mind, let's talk&nbsp;
about how we can get this invoice application&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.160 --> 00:02:05.600
back up and running. Now let's think about the&nbsp;
key data sources for our invoicing application.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.320 --> 00:02:09.200
Let's start with events, and metrics,

00:02:13.040 --> 00:02:22.320
logs, alerts, and a few others but for now&nbsp;
let's focus on these data sources&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.320 --> 00:02:27.280
for our specific invoicing application. In the real&nbsp;
world this will look different depending on your&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.280 --> 00:02:32.480
application architecture, the type of data sources&nbsp;
that are applicable for your application, and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.480 --> 00:02:38.640
data regulatory requirements. So we've got our key&nbsp;
data sources, now how does this fit into our model&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.640 --> 00:02:49.840
for AIOps? Let's think about three key steps. The&nbsp;
first one we're going to call monitor and discover.

00:02:52.080 --> 00:02:56.800
So in this first step the data is&nbsp;
ingested by the AIOps platform,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.800 --> 00:03:01.520
and is thresholded and creates&nbsp;
baselines for your specific application.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.080 --> 00:03:06.720
So let's think about it this way what&nbsp;
is normal for my invoicing application?

00:03:06.720 --> 00:03:12.640
What is the log ingestion rate, how many errors&nbsp;
is acceptable based on our slo, or service level&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.640 --> 00:03:24.960
objective? So we now have that information, the next&nbsp;
step of the process is about engage and context.

00:03:28.080 --> 00:03:33.920
So the next step is engage in context.&nbsp;
So this is where AIOps really shines&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.560 --> 00:03:40.240
it takes all of that ingested data, and it&nbsp;
surfaces it to an IT operations professional&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.240 --> 00:03:45.840
or site reliability engineer in the form of a&nbsp;
collaboration solution, also known as chat ops.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.480 --> 00:03:50.640
So up until now everything's been done in the&nbsp;
background and as soon as this incident pops&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.640 --> 00:03:55.520
up with our invoicing application it surfaced&nbsp;
via chat ops to our site reliability engineer.&nbsp;

00:03:56.080 --> 00:04:01.120
Less is more here they have the context on&nbsp;
where the incident is located in the application,

00:04:01.680 --> 00:04:06.160
what specific actions are recommended&nbsp;
to resolve this, and most importantly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.160 --> 00:04:10.720
how are those actions based on incidents&nbsp;
like this that have come up in the past?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:11.760 --> 00:04:22.240
So now our sre is armed with that information,&nbsp;
and it's our last phase which is act and automate.

00:04:24.640 --> 00:04:30.080
So everything's been done in the background, this&nbsp;
information has been surfaced to our IT officer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:30.080 --> 00:04:36.640
sre, ITOps professional sre, and then finally we&nbsp;
have to act and automate to resolve this issue.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:38.160 --> 00:04:43.200
The suggested options that are available via&nbsp;
chat ops enable the ITOps to select what has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:43.200 --> 00:04:48.640
worked in the past and with a click activate&nbsp;
a script or run book to resolve this issue&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:48.640 --> 00:04:53.600
as soon as it's detected. This gets our&nbsp;
invoicing application back up and running faster&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:53.600 --> 00:04:57.360
and make sure that our partners&nbsp;
are happier with this experience.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.080 --> 00:05:03.760
So now we've got the overview, three key steps,&nbsp;
the type of data that's ingested by AIOps.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:04.480 --> 00:05:09.600
In summary this system allows its&nbsp;
professionals to solve problems faster,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:09.600 --> 00:05:13.360
to keep applications up and running, and&nbsp;
help protect the business in the long run.&nbsp;&nbsp;

